config BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_SH8601
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3 1.43\" Round AMOLED (SH8601/CO5300 466x466)"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
    help
        The Waveshare 1.43" round AMOLED board ships with either an
        SH8601 or a CO5300 driver IC — both speak the same QSPI
        protocol, so the same panel driver works for either. Folder/
        symbol naming follows the Espressif managed component
        (`esp_lcd_sh8601`) we actually link against.

config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DEMO
    bool "AMOLED driver-verification demo (no Wi-Fi, static test pattern)"
    default n
    depends on BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_SH8601
    help
        When enabled, app_main bypasses NVS / Wi-Fi / HTTP / NTP entirely
        and just renders a static test pattern (color bars + corner
        markers + centre crosshair) on the AMOLED. Use this to verify
        the SH8601/CO5300 panel driver: SLPOUT/DISPON, RGB565 byte order,
        and the CASET/RASET column/row offsets. Disable for normal builds.

menu "AMOLED burn-in mitigation"
    depends on BURNSCOPE_DISPLAY_AMOLED_SH8601

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_DIM_MINUTES
        int "Minutes of idle before dimming the panel"
        default 5
        range 1 60
        help
            After this many minutes with no activity event (motion,
            touch, button, or qualifying POST /summary push) the
            burn-in adapter dims the panel from
            BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT down to
            BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DIMMED_BRIGHTNESS_PCT. See
            docs/fsd/oled-burn-in-mitigation-fsd.md § A2.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_OFF_MINUTES
        int "Minutes of idle before turning the panel off"
        default 30
        range 1 240
        help
            After this many minutes idle the burn-in adapter issues
            DISPOFF (MIPI DCS 0x28). The HTTP server keeps running so
            an incoming push wakes the panel within ~200 ms. Must be
            >= BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_IDLE_DIM_MINUTES; equal values mean
            "no dim phase, jump straight to off."

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT
        int "Active-state brightness, % of panel maximum"
        default 70
        range 0 100
        help
            Brightness used in the ACTIVE state, as a percentage of
            the SH8601 / CO5300 0x51 register's 8-bit range. The 70 %
            default matches the catalog's recommended luminance cap.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_DIMMED_BRIGHTNESS_PCT
        int "Dimmed-state brightness, % of panel maximum"
        default 20
        range 0 100
        help
            Brightness used in the DIMMED state. Should be <=
            BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_ACTIVE_BRIGHTNESS_PCT. Set to 0 to make
            the dim phase visually identical to off (panel still
            powered).

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_MOTION_THRESHOLD_MG
        int "Motion-wake threshold (milli-g)"
        default 50
        range 1 2000
        help
            Per-sample accelerometer delta-magnitude (mg) that the
            QMI8658 sampler treats as motion. Consumed by the PR-2
            IMU adapter; carried in the burn_idle config struct so
            the SM and adapter share one configuration record.

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_WAKE_FADE_MS
        int "Brightness fade-up duration (ms)"
        default 300
        range 0 5000
        help
            Duration of the linear brightness ramp when the panel is
            waking or transitioning to a brighter state (OFF→DIMMED,
            OFF→ACTIVE, DIMMED→ACTIVE). The SH8601/CO5300 has no
            hardware fade primitive, so the adapter writes intermediate
            0x51 register values at ~30 Hz over this interval. Set to 0
            for instantaneous wake (legacy behavior).

    config BURNSCOPE_AMOLED_SLEEP_FADE_MS
        int "Brightness fade-down duration (ms)"
        default 1500
        range 0 5000
        help
            Duration of the linear brightness ramp when the panel is
            dimming or powering down (ACTIVE→DIMMED, DIMMED→OFF,
            ACTIVE→OFF). For DIMMED→OFF transitions the DISPOFF command
            runs after the fade reaches 0. Set to 0 for instantaneous
            dim/off (legacy behavior).

endmenu
